tion ${y}^{′}(1)=0.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =6{c}_{1}{t}^{5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{5}+6{c}_{2}{t}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=0$ and ${c}_{1}=4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =6{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 0 & =24+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =4{t}^{6}-24{t}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\  & =4{t}^{6}(1-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536001 true] [17592186378973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378974 13194139536001 true] [17592186378973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378975 13194139536001 true] [17592186378973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378976 13194139536001 true] [17592186378973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378977 13194139536001 true] [17592186378973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378978 13194139536001 true] [17592186378973 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536001 true] [17592186378973 1041 "selection" 13194139536001 true] [17592186378973 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378976 13194139536001 true] [17592186378973 1110 #uuid "652fea83-9d0b-5116-98f7-7888a0cdc8e7" 13194139536001 true] [17592186378974 1034 "y(t)={t}^{6}(4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" 13194139536001 true] [17592186378974 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536001 true] [17592186378974 1111 #uuid "0ca6c1d1-1567-55b7-832d-8bd712e03db7" 13194139536001 true] [17592186378975 1034 "y(t)=4{t}^{6}(2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" 13194139536001 true] [17592186378975 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536001 true] [17592186378975 1111 #uuid "147e8823-878b-5498-b950-99730bd477e7" 13194139536001 true] [17592186378976 1034 "y(t)=4{t}^{6}(1-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" 13194139536001 true] [17592186378976 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536001 true] [17592186378976 1111 #uuid "6108fd89-8009-58e0-ae2f-869365c89ce3" 13194139536001 true] [17592186378977 1034 "y(t)=2{t}^{-6}(1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" 13194139536001 true] [17592186378977 1103 #edb/ref 17592